      "doc": "Empty, or one datum in Avro single-object encoding: the marker C3 01, the 8-byte little-endian CRC-64-AVRO fingerprint of the datum's writer schema, then the datum in Avro binary encoding."
    },
    {
      "name": "signature",
      "type": {
        "type": "fixed",
        "name": "Signature",
        "size": 64,
        "doc": "An Ed25519 signature. Defined in spec/keys.md."
      },
      "doc": "The sender's signature over the message. What it covers is defined in spec/keys.md."
    }
  ]
}
''',
  'axt.Error': r'''
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "Error",
  "namespace": "axt",
  "doc": "The body of an ERROR message: a message the receiver could not process, and why. Defined in spec/protocol.md. Its schema changes only with a new envelope format.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "to",
      "type": {
        "type": "fixed",
        "name": "ErrorTo",
        "size": 32,
        "doc": "An Ed25519 public key in the encoding of RFC 8032. Defined in spec/keys.md."
      },
      "doc": "The Ed25519 public key of the device that sent the reported message: in a live connection the key its HELLO proved, through a relay the key that signed the message. A device ignores an error that names another key."
    },
    {
      "name": "code",
      "type": {
        "type": "enum",
        "name": "ErrorCode",
        "doc": "Why the receiver could not process the message; spec/protocol.md defines each code. INVALID_MESSAGE: not a valid message of its kind. FORMAT_UNSUPPORTED: an envelope format the receiver does not read. TOO_LARGE: above a size limit of spec/envelope.md. SIGNATURE_INVALID: the signature does not verify. MANIFEST_INVALID: an invalid manifest. OFFER_INVALID: an invalid offer. RECORD_ID_INVALID: an invalid record id. VERSION_INVALID: a version below 1. SCHEMA_UNKNOWN: a fingerprint the receiver has no schema for. NOT_ACCEPTED: a record message without an accepted offer of its type. TYPE_CHANGED: a record under another type than before. UNDECODABLE: a record body that cannot be decoded. DEVICE_REJECTED: a DEVICE_JOIN, DEVICE_ADD or DEVICE_REMOVE the receiver did not apply, as spec/keys.md, section 5, defines. VALUE_INVALID: a record that decodes but holds a value that breaks a rule of its type, named in field. RECORD_UNKNOWN: a CHANGE that does not hold the whole record, for a record the receiver does not have or holds only its removal. PROPOSALS_NOT_TAKEN: a PROPOSAL for a record whose sender takes none from the proposer. The default is for schema resolution only; within one envelope format every symbol is known.",
        "symbols": [
          "INVALID_MESSAGE",
          "FORMAT_UNSUPPORTED",
          "TOO_LARGE",
          "SIGNATURE_INVALID",
          "MANIFEST_INVALID",
          "OFFER_INVALID",
          "RECORD_ID_INVALID",
          "VERSION_INVALID",
          "SCHEMA_UNKNOWN",
          "NOT_ACCEPTED",
          "TYPE_CHANGED",
          "UNDECODABLE",
          "DEVICE_REJECTED",
          "VALUE_INVALID",
          "RECORD_UNKNOWN",
          "PROPOSALS_NOT_TAKEN"
        ],
        "default": "INVALID_MESSAGE"
      },
      "doc": "Why the receiver could not process the message."
    },
    {
      "name": "message_hash",
      "type": {
        "type": "fixed",
        "name": "ErrorMessageHash",
        "size": 32,
        "doc": "A SHA-256 hash."
      },
      "doc": "The SHA-256 of the reported message as the receiver got it, from its single-object marker to its last byte; through a relay, after opening and removing the padding."
    },
    {
      "name": "record",
      "type": [
        "null",
        {
          "type": "record",
          "name": "ErrorRecord",
          "doc": "The record field of the reported message.",
          "fields": [
            {
              "name": "id",
              "type": "string",
              "doc": "The id as the reported message carried it, which may not be a valid UUID."
            },
            {
              "name": "version",
              "type": "long",
              "doc": "The version as the reported message carried it, which may be below 1."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "doc": "The record field of the reported message, when its signature verified, it carried one and its id is at most 64 bytes long. Null otherwise."
    },
    {
      "name": "fingerprint",
      "type": [
        "null",
        {
          "type": "fixed",
          "name": "ErrorFingerprint",
          "size": 8,
          "doc": "A CRC-64-AVRO fingerprint, 8 bytes in little-endian order, as spec/envelope.md defines."
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "doc": "The fingerprint the code is about, as spec/protocol.md says for the code: for SCHEMA_UNKNOWN, that of the schema the receiver lacks; for FORMAT_UNSUPPORTED, the fingerprint of the envelope. Null for every other code."
    },
    {
      "name": "field",
      "type": [
        "null",
        "string"
      ],
      "default": null,
      "doc": "For VALUE_INVALID, the path of the value that breaks a rule, by the field names of the offered schema, as spec/metadata.md defines it: an empty string for the record itself. Null for every other code, and for a path above 1024 bytes."
    },
    {
      "name": "detail",
      "type": "string",
      "default": "",
      "doc": "A description for logs, in English, as plain text on one line of at most 1024 bytes. Empty when there is none. It is not shown to the user as the only explanation."
    }
  ]
}
''',
  'axt.Forward': r'''
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "Forward",
  "namespace": "axt",
  "doc": "The body of a FORWARD message: one message of another app, passed on by a device to another device of its own sender. Defined in spec/sync.md. The envelope's record field names the forward: its id is an id of the forward, not of a record, and its version is 1. The device that gets it verifies the signature of the message inside, processes that message as if it had received it, sends nothing to the app that signed it, and acknowledges the forward. Its schema changes only with a new envelope format.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "to",
      "type": {
        "type": "fixed",
        "name": "ForwardTo",
        "size": 32,
        "doc": "An Ed25519 public key in the encoding of RFC 8032. Defined in spec/keys.md."
      },
      "doc": "The Ed25519 public key of the device the message is for, another current device of the sender's own device set. A device ignores a FORWARD that names another key."
    },
    {
      "name": "message",
      "type": "bytes",
      "doc": "One complete message of another app, as the forwarding device received it: the single-object marker, the fingerprint of the envelope schema and the envelope in binary encoding, with the signature of the app that sent it. A MANIFEST, a DATA, a DELETE, a DEVICE_ADD or a DEVICE_REMOVE, or a message of another kind whose document says that it is forwarded. Its bytes are passed on unchanged."
    },
    {
      "name": "schema",
      "type": [
        "null",
        "string"
      ],
      "default": null,
      "doc": "For a forwarded DATA, the writer schema of its body as its full JSON text, as the app that sent the DATA offered it or, for a DATA that the device read in a file, as the file's axt.schemas holds it; its fingerprint is the one the body of the DATA names. Null for every other forwarded message."
    }
  ]
}
''',
  'axt.Manifest': r'''
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "Manifest",
  "namespace": "axt",
  "doc": "The types an app takes and what it does with them; the body of a MANIFEST message. Defined in spec/manifest.md. Its schema changes only with a new envelope format.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "revision",
      "type": "long",
      "doc": "The revision of this manifest, at least 1. It rises with every change of the manifest's content, so that a receiver can tell the latest of several manifests of the same app apart from older ones."
    },
    {
      "name": "app_name",
      "type": "string",
      "doc": "The name the app gives itself, as plain text on one line, such as Old Brain Fix. It is shown to the other app's user; it does not identify the app, the keys of its sender do, of which the sender key of the envelope is one."
    },
    {
      "name": "app_url",
      "type": [
        "null",
        "string"
      ],
      "default": null,
      "doc": "An absolute https URL of a page about the app. Null when the app names none."
    },
    {
      "name": "formats",
      "type": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": "int"
      },
      "doc": "The envelope formats the app reads, each at least 1, without duplicates. It includes the format of the envelope that carries this manifest."
    },
    {
      "name": "takes",
      "type": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "record",
          "name": "ManifestTake",
          "doc": "One type the app takes, the versions of it it takes, and what it does with its records.",
          "fields": [
            {
              "name": "type",
              "type": "string",
              "doc": "The full name of the type, namespace and name, such as axt.example.v1.Appointment. Matched exactly; the major version is part of the name."
            },
            {
              "name": "min_version",
              "type": "int",
              "doc": "The lowest version of the type the app takes, as the type's axt.version attribute numbers it; at least 1. A schema without a valid axt.version counts as version 1."
            },
            {
              "name": "max_version",
              "type": [
                "null",
                "int"
              ],
              "default": null,
              "doc": "The highest version of the type the app takes, at least min_version. Null when the app takes every version from min_version on."
            },
            {
              "name": "purpose",
              "type": "string",
              "doc": "One sentence in English, plain text on one line, on what the app does with records of the type, such as: An Appointment becomes a Reminder."
            },
            {
              "name": "purpose_translations",
              "type": {
                "type": "map",
                "values": "string"
              },
              "default": {},
              "doc": "The sentence of the field purpose in other languages. Each key is a BCP 47 language tag other than en, such as de or pt-BR; each value is the sentence in that language, plain text on one line. Empty when there are none."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "default": [],
      "doc": "The types the app takes, each full name at most once. Empty when the app takes no type by name."
    },
    {
      "name": "any_type",
      "type": [
        "null",
        {
          "type": "record",
          "name": "ManifestAnyType",
          "doc": "That the app takes every type that takes does not name, in every version, and what it does with their records.",
          "fields": [
            {
              "name": "purpose",
              "type": "string",
              "doc": "One sentence in English, plain text on one line, on what the app does with records of a type that takes does not name, such as: Any other type becomes a searchable Note."
            },
            {
              "name": "purpose_translations",
              "type": {
                "type": "map",
                "values": "string"
              },
              "default": {},
              "doc": "The sentence of the field purpose in other languages, keyed by BCP 47 language tag other than en, as in ManifestTake. Empty when there are none."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "doc": "Whether the app takes every type that takes does not name. Null when it takes only the types in takes."
    },
    {
      "name": "sends",
      "type": [
        "null",
        {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "record",
            "name": "ManifestSend",
            "doc": "One type the app may send, the versions of it it writes, and whether it takes proposals for its records of the type.",
            "fields": [
              {
                "name": "type",
                "type": "string",
                "doc": "The full name of the type, namespace and name, such as axt.example.v1.Pet."
              },
              {
                "name": "min_version",
                "type": "int",
                "doc": "The lowest version of the type the app writes, as the type's axt.version attribute numbers it; at least 1. A schema without a valid axt.version counts as version 1."
              },
              {
                "name": "max_version",
                "type": [
                  "null",
                  "int"
                ],
                "default": null,
                "doc": "The highest version of the type the app writes, at least min_version. Null when the app does not say."
              },
              {
                "name": "proposals",
                "type": "boolean",
                "default": false,
                "doc": "Whether the app takes proposals of changes to the records of this type it sends, as PROPOSAL messages. False when it takes none."
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "doc": "The types the app may send, each full name at most once; for display only. Null when the app does not say; empty when it sends no type."
    },
    {
      "name": "encryption_key",
      "type": [
        "null",
        {
          "type": "fixed",
          "name": "ManifestEncryptionKey",
          "size": 32,
          "doc": "An X25519 public key in the encoding of RFC 7748. Defined in spec/keys.md."
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "doc": "The X25519 public key of this installation with which other apps encrypt messages to it through a relay, as spec/keys.md defines. Null when the app takes no messages through a relay."
    },
    {
      "name": "relay",
      "type": [
        "null",
        {
          "type": "record",
          "name": "ManifestRelay",
          "doc": "The relay and the mailbox at it into which other apps put messages for this installation. Defined in spec/transports.md.",
          "fields": [
            {
              "name": "url",
              "type": "string",
              "doc": "The base URL of the relay: an absolute https URL with a host, ending with a slash, without user information, query or fragment, at most 256 bytes, such as https://relay.example.org/axt/. The paths of the relay's interface are appended to it."
            },
            {
              "name": "mailbox",
              "type": {
                "type": "fixed",
                "name": "ManifestRelayMailbox",
                "size": 32,
                "doc": "A mailbox id: the SHA-256 of a fixed prefix and the mailbox secret that only the mailbox's owner holds. Defined in spec/transports.md."
              },
              "doc": "The id of the mailbox at the relay into which other apps put messages for this installation."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "doc": "Where other apps put messages for this installation through a relay. Null when the app takes no messages through a relay; it is present exactly when encryption_key is."
    }
  ]
}
''',
  'axt.Offer': r'''
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "Offer",
  "namespace": "axt",
  "doc": "The body of an OFFER message: the types, each with its writer schema, whose records the sender wants to send to one receiver. Defined in spec/protocol.md. Its schema changes only with a new envelope format.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "to",
      "type": {
        "type": "fixed",
        "name": "OfferTo",
        "size": 32,
        "doc": "An Ed25519 public key in the encoding of RFC 8032. Defined in spec/keys.md."
      },
      "doc": "The Ed25519 public key of the device the offer is made to, a current key of the receiver. A device ignores an offer that names another key."
    },
    {
      "name": "offer_id",
      "type": {
        "type": "string",
        "logicalType": "uuid"
      },
      "doc": "The id of the offer, a version 4 or 7 UUID in its 36-character lower-case text form, which the sender never uses for another offer. The answers to the offer name it."
    },
    {
      "name": "types",
      "type": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "record",
          "name": "OfferType",
          "doc": "One type the sender offers, with the writer schema of its records.",
          "fields": [
            {
              "name": "schema",
              "type": "string",
              "doc": "The writer schema of the type as its full JSON text, doc attributes and axt.version included, with which the sender writes the records it sends under this offer. The type's full name and version are those of this schema."
            },
            {
              "name": "count",
              "type": "long",
              "default": 0,
              "doc": "The number of record messages of the type, DATA and DELETE together, that the sender is about to send under this offer; for display only. 0 when the sender does not say."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "doc": "The types offered, 1 to 256, each full name and each fingerprint at most once."
    }
  ]
}
''',
  'axt.Proposal': r'''
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "Proposal",
  "namespace": "axt",
  "doc": "The body of a PROPOSAL message: a receiver of a record proposes changed values of some of its fields to the record's sender, whose user takes or refuses them. Defined in spec/shares.md. The envelope's record field names the sender's record and the version of it that the proposer holds; no version rule applies to the message. The proposal changes nothing by itself: a value the sender's user takes reaches every receiver as an ordinary update. Its schema changes only with a new envelope format.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "to",
      "type": {
        "type": "fixed",
        "name": "ProposalTo",
        "size": 32,
        "doc": "An Ed25519 public key in the encoding of RFC 8032. Defined in spec/keys.md."
      },
      "doc": "The Ed25519 public key of the device of the record's sender that the proposal is sent to, a current key of that sender. A device that gets it directly ignores a PROPOSAL that names another key; a forwarded one is rejected unless this is a current or a removed key of the device's own set."
    },
    {
      "name": "proposal_id",
      "type": {
        "type": "string",
        "logicalType": "uuid"
      },
      "doc": "The id of the proposal, a version 4 or 7 UUID in its 36-character lower-case text form, which the proposer never uses for another proposal and which is not the id of a record, an offer, a request or a forward. The reply to the proposal names it."
    },
    {
      "name": "fields",
      "type": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "record",
          "name": "ProposalField",
          "doc": "The proposed value of one top-level field of the record. Defined in spec/shares.md, section 13.1.",
          "fields": [
            {
              "name": "name",
              "type": "string",
              "doc": "The name of the field, as the writer schema named in schema has it."
            },
            {
              "name": "schema",
              "type": {
                "type": "fixed",
                "name": "ProposalFieldSchema",
                "size": 8,
                "doc": "The CRC-64-AVRO fingerprint of a schema, as 8 bytes in little-endian order. Defined in spec/envelope.md, section 5."
              },
              "doc": "The fingerprint of the writer schema of the record's type with which the proposer wrote the value: the writer schema of the record's kept DATA, with which the proposer's change of the field was written. The owner keeps the writer schemas of the DATA it sent to the receiver."
            },
            {
              "name": "value",
              "type": "bytes",
              "doc": "The proposed value of the field, in Avro binary encoding under the type the field has in the schema named in schema."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "doc": "The proposed values, 1 to 4096, each field name at most once, in any order. Only fields that the proposal changes; a proposal neither creates nor deletes a record."
    }
  ]
}
''',
  'axt.ProposalReply': r'''
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "ProposalReply",
  "namespace": "axt",
  "doc": "The body of a PROPOSAL_REPLY message: the answer of a record's sender to one proposal, taken or refused by its user. Defined in spec/shares.md. The envelope's record field is that of the proposal. The reply is a status only: a proposal that is taken reaches the proposer as an ordinary update of the record. Its schema changes only with a new envelope format.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "to",
      "type": {
        "type": "fixed",
        "name": "ProposalReplyTo",
        "size": 32,
        "doc": "An Ed25519 public key in the encoding of RFC 8032. Defined in spec/keys.md."
      },
      "doc": "The Ed25519 public key that signed the proposal, the key of the proposer's device that sent it. A device ignores a reply that names another key."
    },
    {
      "name": "proposal_id",
      "type": {
        "type": "string",
        "logicalType": "uuid"
      },
      "doc": "The id of the proposal this message answers, as the proposal carried it."
    },
    {
      "name": "answer",
      "type": {
        "type": "enum",
        "name": "ProposalReplyAnswer",
        "doc": "What the sender's user did with the proposal. ACCEPTED: took every proposed value into the record, which reaches the proposer as an update. DECLINED: did not take the proposal as it stands. The default is for schema resolution only; within one envelope format every symbol is known.",
        "symbols": [
          "ACCEPTED",
          "DECLINED"
        ],
        "default": "DECLINED"
      },
      "doc": "The answer to the proposal."
    }
  ]
}
''',
  'axt.QrPayload': r'''
